# Example configuration for attn.
#
# Copy to `.env` and edit. Every value below is optional and shown with its
# default. Bun auto-loads `.env` from the working directory for both
# `bun run dev` and `bun run serve`, so no separate dotenv step is needed.
#
# Installed (e.g. Homebrew) deployments don't use this file: the packaged
# `attn` binary sets ATTN_HOME, and the app then reads the same
# KEY=value format from ~/.config/attn/env instead (state moves to
# ~/.local/state/attn/, the review prompt override to
# ~/.config/attn/review.md). Precedence everywhere: process environment >
# config file > default.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file must never contain secrets. GitHub authentication comes
# from your local `gh` CLI, not from here — run:
#
#     gh auth login --hostname <your-host>
#
# and this tool reuses that session (read-only).

# --- Target GitHub host -------------------------------------------------------
# The GitHub (Enterprise) host to query. Defaults to public GitHub. Set this to
# your GHE host, e.g. ghe.example.com. Passed to `gh` as GH_HOST.
# ATTN_HOST=github.com

# --- Relevance filters --------------------------------------------------------
# By default every review-requested PR and every assigned/mentioned issue is
# shown. Narrow the feed with either or both of the filters below; an item is
# kept if it matches ANY repo OR ANY label. Leave both unset to show all.
#
# Exact repo allowlist (bare name or owner/repo). Only PRs and issues in these
# repos are shown; remove a line to drop a repo, add one to include it.
# ATTN_REPOS=
#
# Comma-separated issue/PR labels, e.g. My Team,needs-review
# ATTN_LABELS=

# --- Local checkout discovery -------------------------------------------------
# Directories scanned for local git clones of matched repos, so the dashboard
# can hand a PR to a local agent review. Comma-separated absolute paths.
# Defaults to the working directory.
# ATTN_CHECKOUT_ROOTS=/path/to/your/workspace
#
# Explicit repo -> local-path overrides as JSON, keyed by `owner/repo`. Merged
# ahead of (and taking precedence over) the scanned roots above.
# ATTN_REPO_PATH_MAP={"owner/example-repo":"/abs/path/to/example-repo"}
#
# Working directory the server treats as its base. Defaults to the process CWD.
# ATTN_WORKSPACE=

# --- Local review handoff -----------------------------------------------------
# Markdown template for the code-review prompt handed to a local agent. Defaults
# to ./prompts/review.md. Edit that file (or point this elsewhere) to customize
# the review instructions; see the README for the available {{placeholders}}.
# ATTN_REVIEW_PROMPT_FILE=./prompts/review.md
#
# macOS app used to open the "review terminal" (must handle .command files),
# e.g. Terminal, iTerm, Ghostty. Unset uses the system default handler.
# ATTN_TERMINAL_APP=Terminal

# --- Server -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Port for the local dashboard (binds to 127.0.0.1 only). Unlike the settings
# above, the port is consumed BEFORE the app starts: the install scripts bake it
# into the LaunchAgent plist (they read this file, so setting it here is enough),
# and `bun run dev` / `bun run serve` take it from your shell. So for a manual
# run, export it — `ATTN_PORT=8791 bun run serve` — because those scripts
# expand it before bun loads this file. Changing it here means re-running
# scripts/install-service.sh to apply it to the installed service.
# ATTN_PORT=8765
#
# Seconds between background poll cycles.
# ATTN_POLL_SECONDS=900

# --- Local state file paths ---------------------------------------------------
# Where user intent, the gh cache, and the last snapshot are stored. Defaults
# live under .local-state/ (git-ignored). Override only if you need them
# elsewhere.
# ATTN_STATE_FILE=
# ATTN_SNAPSHOT_FILE=
# ATTN_CACHE_FILE=

# --- Search + enrichment limits -----------------------------------------------
# Max PRs returned by the PR search.
# ATTN_LIMIT=50
#
# Max issues returned by each issue search.
# ATTN_ISSUE_LIMIT=25
#
# Number of issues enriched with their comments (0 disables comment enrichment).
# ATTN_ISSUE_COMMENT_ITEM_LIMIT=5
#
# Latest comments (and PR review submissions) kept per item (0 disables comment
# items entirely).
# ATTN_COMMENTS_PER_ISSUE=3

# --- Cache TTLs (seconds) -----------------------------------------------------
# Keep the search TTLs below ATTN_POLL_SECONDS (default 900) or a poll
# serves the previous search from cache and new items surface an interval late.
# ATTN_PR_SEARCH_TTL_SECONDS=600
# ATTN_ISSUE_SEARCH_TTL_SECONDS=600
# ATTN_PR_VIEW_TTL_SECONDS=1800
# ATTN_ISSUE_VIEW_TTL_SECONDS=3600

# --- Rate-limit handling ------------------------------------------------------
# Cooldown after a GitHub rate-limit response before the next refresh is allowed.
# ATTN_RATE_LIMIT_BACKOFF_SECONDS=900
